.\" Automatically generated by Pandoc 3.5
.\"
.TH "tpm2tss\-genkey" "1" "OCTOBER 2020" "tpm2\-tss\-engine" "General Commands Manual"
.SH "نام (NAME)"
\f[B]tpm2tss\-genkey\f[R](1) \[en] generate TPM keys for
tpm2\-tss\-engine
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
\f[B]tpm2tss\-genkey\f[R] [\f[I]options\f[R]] <\f[I]filename\f[R]>
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
\f[B]tpm2tss\-genkey\f[R] creates a key inside a TPM 2.0 connected via
the tpm2tss software stack.
Those keys may be an RSA key for decryption or signing or an ECC key for
ECDSA signatures.
.PP
The tool respects the OPENSSL_CONF option for specifying engine specific
control parameters.
See \f[CR]man(5) config\f[R] for details on openssl config files.
.SH ARGUMENTS
The \f[CR]tpm2tss\-genkey\f[R] command expects a filename for storing
the resulting TPM key information.
This file can then be loaded with OpenSSL using
\f[CR]openssl pkeyutl \-engine tpm2tss \-keyform engine \-inkey <filename>\f[R].
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]\-a <algorithm>\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-alg <algorithm>\f[R]: The public
key algorithm (rsa, ecdsa) (default: rsa)
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]\-c <curve>\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-curve <curve>\f[R]: If alg ecdsa is
chosen, the curve for ecc (default: nist_p256)
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]\-u <file>\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-public <file>\f[R]: Public key
(TPM2B_PUBLIC) to be imported.
Requires \f[CR]\-r\f[R].
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]\-r <file>\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-private <file>\f[R]: The (encrypted)
private key (TPM2B_PRIVATE) to be imported.
Requires \f[CR]\-u\f[R].
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]\-e <exponent>\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-exponent <exponent>\f[R]: If alg
rsa is chosen, the exponent for rsa (default: 65537)
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]\-h\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-help\f[R]: Print help
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]\-o <password>\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-ownerpw <password>\f[R]: Password
for the owner hierarchy (default: none) Openssl Config control command:
\f[CR]SET_OWNERAUTH\f[R]
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]\-p <password>\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-password <password>\f[R]: Password
for the created key (default: none)
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]\-P <handle>\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-parent <handle>\f[R]: Specific handle
for the parent key (default: none)
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]\-s <keysize>\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-keysize <keysize>\f[R]: If alg rsa
is chosen, the key size in bits (default: 2048)
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]\-v\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-verbose\f[R]: Print verbose messages
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]\-W <password>\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-parentpw <password>\f[R]: Password
for the parent key (default: none) Openssl Config control command:
\f[CR]SET_PARENTAUTH\f[R]
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]\-t <tcti\-conf>\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-tcti <tcti\-conf>\f[R]: TCTI
Configuration string (default: none) Openssl Config control command:
\f[CR]SET_TCTI\f[R]
.SH "مثال‌ها (EXAMPLES)"
Engine information can be retrieved using:
.IP
.EX
$ openssl engine \-t \-c tpm2tss
.EE
.PP
The following sequence of commands creates an RSA key using the TPM,
exports the public key, encrypts a data file and decrypts it using the
TPM:
.IP
.EX
$ tpm2tss\-genkey \-a rsa \-s 2048 mykey
$ openssl rsa \-engine tpm2tss \-inform engine \-in mykey \-pubout \-outform pem \-out mykey.pub
$ openssl pkeyutl \-pubin \-inkey mykey.pub \-in mydata \-encrypt \-out mycipher
$ openssl pkeyutl \-engine tpm2tss \-keyform engine \-inkey mykey \-decrypt \-in mycipher \-out mydata
.EE
.PP
The following sequence of commands creates an RSA key using the TPM,
exports the public key, signs a data file using the TPM and validates
the signature:
.IP
.EX
$ tpm2tss\-genkey \-a rsa \-s 2048 mykey
$ openssl rsa \-engine tpm2tss \-inform engine \-in mykey \-pubout \-outform pem \-out mykey.pub
$ openssl pkeyutl \-engine tpm2tss \-keyform engine \-inkey mykey \-sign \-in mydata \-out mysig
$ openssl pkeyutl \-engine tpm2tss \-keyform engine \-inkey mykey \-verify \-in mydata \-sigfile mysig
.EE
.PP
The following sequence of commands creates an ECDSA key using the TPM,
exports the public key, signs a data file using the TPM and validates
the signature:
.IP
.EX
$ tpm2tss\-genkey \-a ecdsa \-c nist_p256 mykey
$ openssl pkeyutl \-engine tpm2tss \-keyform engine \-inkey mykey \-sign \-in mydata \-out mysig
$ openssl pkeyutl \-engine tpm2tss \-keyform engine \-inkey mykey \-verify \-in mydata \-sigfile mysig
.EE
.SH RETURNS
0 on success or 1 on failure.
